WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:03.830
- This week I'm joined by
Evelyn because this week it is--

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:04.663
- Chocolate!

00:00:04.663 --> 00:00:05.496
- Chocolate.

00:00:05.496 --> 00:00:06.329
- Who doesn't like chocolate?

00:00:06.329 --> 00:00:07.162
- Yeah, who doesn't like chocolate?

00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:09.671
We'll try three different
chocolates at drastically

00:00:09.671 --> 00:00:11.187
different price points to determine

00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:13.486
which is the most worth it.

00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:14.319
- [Female Voice] UK

00:00:14.319 --> 00:00:15.152
(ding)

00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:17.752
- If you lie all the
tire irons in the world

00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:20.835
back to back some of them would sink.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.353
- It is lovely, look at all of this.

00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:26.879
(upbeat music)

00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:29.061
- We're in Arlow, bam! (laughing)

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:29.894
- [Evelyn] We're running late.

00:00:29.894 --> 00:00:32.624
(cash register dings)

00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:33.457
- Hi.

00:00:33.457 --> 00:00:35.314
- Hi, how are you doing?

00:00:35.314 --> 00:00:37.207
Woke up with the idea that I would take

00:00:37.207 --> 00:00:38.311
bars we enjoyed as children,

00:00:38.311 --> 00:00:41.561
but remake them with great ingredients.

00:00:46.243 --> 00:00:47.466
(upbeat music)

00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:49.699
My name's James Ecclestone
and I'm the founder of

00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:50.733
The Grown Up Chocolate
Company and we're expanding

00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:52.895
in my production kitchens in Harlow.

00:00:52.895 --> 00:00:54.520
We have the very best ingredients.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.946
We're making an indulgent treat.

00:00:55.946 --> 00:00:57.980
We're handmade, with focus on the quality

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.124
of what you're doing.

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:01.128
- [Rich] So it truly
is a handmade process.

00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:02.864
Did you just get that off a tray?

00:01:02.864 --> 00:01:03.932
- (questioning noise)

00:01:03.932 --> 00:01:05.356
- We don't mind the chocolate addicts.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:07.521
Salted peanut caramel
is 40% of all our sales.

00:01:07.521 --> 00:01:09.783
The person making a cavity of pear shapes

00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:11.253
and cocoa dark chocolate.

00:01:11.253 --> 00:01:12.776
You make a cavity because
it has to be filled

00:01:12.776 --> 00:01:13.609
with freshly made caramel.

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:15.215
The caramel we make with
concentrated butter,

00:01:15.215 --> 00:01:17.113
full fat cream, the sucrose in sugar.

00:01:17.113 --> 00:01:19.737
Put that caramel in the
bottom of the cavity

00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:22.224
we've made in the chocolate,
add some course sea salts,

00:01:22.224 --> 00:01:24.595
jumbo roasted peanuts,
then we cap it with peanut

00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:27.855
praline, we cap that cavity
with more milk chocolate.

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:30.356
Then we roll it on the
machine behind me and

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.825
it goes through a chocolate waterfall,

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.052
for want of a better word.

00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:35.451
Then he blow off the chocolate
with a hot air dryer,

00:01:35.451 --> 00:01:37.224
after that somebody decorates it with

00:01:37.224 --> 00:01:38.441
the chocolate sprinkles.

00:01:38.441 --> 00:01:40.744
The third person unloading
the tunnel boxes it

00:01:40.744 --> 00:01:43.106
for retail use and off to the destination.

00:01:43.106 --> 00:01:45.355
Today you're gonna be trying
the peanut salted caramel,

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:47.534
retails for about £1.95, (cash register)

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:48.756
a maximum indulgence.

00:01:48.756 --> 00:01:49.589
- Let's do it. (laughing)

00:01:49.589 --> 00:01:50.422
Let's indulge.

00:01:50.422 --> 00:01:51.255
(clap)

00:01:51.255 --> 00:01:53.277
- Nice try kid, but it's not for you.

00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:55.772
Two bars of sumptuous salted caramel.

00:01:55.772 --> 00:01:57.122
What does sumptuous mean?

00:01:57.122 --> 00:01:59.364
- They're like tasty or sexy.

00:01:59.364 --> 00:02:00.880
- [Together] Sexy?

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.200
- [Evelyn] You're sitting
pretty sumptuously right now.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.403
We've seen these go
through the whole process.

00:02:06.403 --> 00:02:09.055
They did a better job on
that one than that one.

00:02:09.055 --> 00:02:11.047
- I guess that's the art
of makin' it by hand,

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:12.435
they're all different.

00:02:12.435 --> 00:02:13.268
- [Rich] Yeah.

00:02:13.268 --> 00:02:14.430
- They're not exactly the same.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.075
- This is a nice, heavy,
solid chocolate, isn't it?

00:02:17.075 --> 00:02:19.278
Oh it's already touched
the mouth I can't cheers.

00:02:19.278 --> 00:02:20.377
(ding)

00:02:20.377 --> 00:02:21.210
Cheers.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.043
- Mmm.

00:02:22.043 --> 00:02:22.876
- Oh wow.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.739
Rich, powerful chocolate.

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:26.663
We have the hard chocolate on the outside,

00:02:26.663 --> 00:02:27.885
perfect milk chocolate.

00:02:27.885 --> 00:02:29.269
- This chocolate is so buttery.

00:02:29.269 --> 00:02:30.287
- Yeah.

00:02:30.287 --> 00:02:31.716
- And it instantly melt in your mouth.

00:02:31.716 --> 00:02:33.508
- The salted caramel,
which really is salted,

00:02:33.508 --> 00:02:34.563
it's not too sweet.

00:02:34.563 --> 00:02:37.051
- Smooth, sticky, nice.

00:02:37.051 --> 00:02:38.644
- That white stuff is the peanut.

00:02:38.644 --> 00:02:40.601
Pure hard-hitting peanut taste, isn't it?

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:41.434
- It is!

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:42.267
- Right?

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:44.551
- Kinda like gritty, slightly salty again.

00:02:44.551 --> 00:02:46.268
Balanced really well chocolate.

00:02:46.268 --> 00:02:51.042
All of the good things
packed into one little bar,

00:02:51.042 --> 00:02:52.649
one big bite.

00:02:52.649 --> 00:02:54.315
- Truly sumptuous.

00:02:54.315 --> 00:02:55.705
The Joe of chocolates.

00:02:55.705 --> 00:02:57.861
- I don't know if I want to eat this now.

00:02:57.861 --> 00:02:58.837
(laughing)

00:02:58.837 --> 00:03:01.456
- So I think this next
place has the coolest name,

00:03:01.456 --> 00:03:05.865
of all places ever:
Choccywoccydoodah in Brighton.

00:03:05.865 --> 00:03:07.945
I just picture working there
and answering the phone.

00:03:07.945 --> 00:03:09.660
Hello, Choccywoccydoodah.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.493
- Aww.

00:03:10.493 --> 00:03:13.411
It kinda sounds like a magical place.

00:03:13.411 --> 00:03:14.244
- Yeah.

00:03:14.244 --> 00:03:16.880
So I used to live in Brighton
and I went away for a week

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.641
and my roommate left my window open.

00:03:18.641 --> 00:03:21.165
And I came back and there
were like twigs on my bed

00:03:21.165 --> 00:03:23.366
and it smelt really weird
and then under my desk

00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:25.073
there was this massive seagull.

00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:25.906
Terrifying.

00:03:25.906 --> 00:03:26.739
(dramatic music)

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.298
Luckily it was fine, but
I would close the widow

00:03:29.298 --> 00:03:31.711
and he would come back and
like hammer on the window

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.099
and look at me like hey you're in my room.

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:34.571
- You stole his house.

00:03:34.571 --> 00:03:35.953
- He stole my house.

00:03:35.953 --> 00:03:38.536
(upbeat music)

00:03:41.671 --> 00:03:44.727
We're here in sunny Brighton,
in the middle of summer.

00:03:44.727 --> 00:03:45.869
- Lovely England.

00:03:45.869 --> 00:03:46.702
- Ahh!

00:03:46.702 --> 00:03:47.812
(dramatic music)

00:03:47.812 --> 00:03:48.645
Oh my God!

00:03:49.482 --> 00:03:50.607
Oh my God!

00:03:50.607 --> 00:03:53.564
- [Evelyn] (laughing)

00:03:53.564 --> 00:03:56.132
- Sh-- (beep)

00:03:56.132 --> 00:03:56.965
- Aww.

00:03:56.965 --> 00:03:58.419
- We've just been mugged
by a pack of thugs.

00:03:58.419 --> 00:03:59.252
(beep)

00:03:59.252 --> 00:04:01.430
Now I'm having a bad hair
day and it's not sunny

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.579
in sunny Brighton.

00:04:02.579 --> 00:04:03.517
- Brighton.

00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:05.653
(cash register ding)

00:04:05.653 --> 00:04:08.849
- The beauty with what we
do is, we stick chocolate

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:10.773
to chocolate with chocolate.

00:04:10.773 --> 00:04:12.819
- So it's like an art gallery, but it's

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.045
all made out of chocolate.

00:04:14.045 --> 00:04:15.714
- It's all 100% edible.

00:04:15.714 --> 00:04:16.853
Pretty fun right?

00:04:16.853 --> 00:04:20.138
So I'm Dan and we're at
Choccywoccydoodah in Brighton.

00:04:20.138 --> 00:04:22.250
We're an art and design
focused chocolatery.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:25.017
We pride ourselves on making cakes

00:04:25.017 --> 00:04:27.174
that like defy gravity.

00:04:27.174 --> 00:04:28.889
- I noticed you called it a chocolatery.

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:30.025
It's not a chocolate shop.

00:04:30.025 --> 00:04:31.022
- Oh we're not gonna throw you out if you

00:04:31.022 --> 00:04:32.215
call us a chocolate shop.

00:04:32.215 --> 00:04:33.155
- What's the difference?

00:04:33.155 --> 00:04:34.363
- Oh, don't ask me that, I don't know.

00:04:34.363 --> 00:04:35.196
Oh dear.

00:04:35.196 --> 00:04:36.029
- It's French.

00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:37.121
- It's French.

00:04:37.121 --> 00:04:40.332
This one here took a team
of four, three days to make.

00:04:40.332 --> 00:04:41.429
- He's holding his thingy.

00:04:41.429 --> 00:04:43.503
- Not all the magic happens here though,

00:04:43.503 --> 00:04:44.563
it is a top-secret location.

00:04:44.563 --> 00:04:45.623
- Do you have Oompa Loompas?

00:04:45.623 --> 00:04:46.844
- We don't have Oompa Loompas.

00:04:46.844 --> 00:04:47.677
- Ah.

00:04:47.677 --> 00:04:48.813
- So today you're gonna be trying our

00:04:48.813 --> 00:04:50.198
Choccywoccyrocky Road.

00:04:50.198 --> 00:04:51.989
It's quite a mouth full as we like to say.

00:04:51.989 --> 00:04:53.057
- Choccywoccyrocky Road.

00:04:53.057 --> 00:04:53.915
Choccywoccyrocky Road.

00:04:53.915 --> 00:04:55.740
Choccywoccyrocky Road.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.966
(laughing)

00:04:56.966 --> 00:04:57.799
- She's a pro.

00:04:57.799 --> 00:04:58.632
- She is a pro.

00:04:58.632 --> 00:05:00.681
Literally everything that's
fantastic on it inside

00:05:00.681 --> 00:05:01.985
and covered in chocolate.

00:05:01.985 --> 00:05:04.470
Nugget, honeycomb, coconut ice, jellybeans

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.093
and marshmallows.

00:05:06.093 --> 00:05:08.705
We mix everything
together in a giant bowl,

00:05:08.705 --> 00:05:10.213
set that in the fridge.

00:05:10.213 --> 00:05:12.910
Once it's set we drizzle it
with molten white chocolate.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.397
Once that's fully set,
we'll take it out and

00:05:15.397 --> 00:05:17.015
then individually wrap each bar,

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:18.566
ready for sale in the shop.

00:05:18.566 --> 00:05:20.907
So today you're gonna be
trying our enormous bar of

00:05:20.907 --> 00:05:22.597
Choccywoccyrocky Road and it's priced at

00:05:22.597 --> 00:05:24.962
(cash register) £29.99.

00:05:24.962 --> 00:05:27.879
- This isn't a bar, this is a slab.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:33.348
It's like unwrapping a
Christmas present and

00:05:33.348 --> 00:05:35.838
you just get hit with the smell.

00:05:35.838 --> 00:05:36.967
(plastic wrapping)

00:05:36.967 --> 00:05:37.989
- [Together] Beast.

00:05:37.989 --> 00:05:39.833
- So beautiful.

00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:40.935
[Together] Ohh!

00:05:40.935 --> 00:05:42.360
- [Evelyn] Look at the marshmallow.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.660
- [Rich] O.M.G.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.800
Right, that's your bit, this is my bit.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:45.633
- What?

00:05:45.633 --> 00:05:48.753
- I can see marshmallow, coconut ice,

00:05:48.753 --> 00:05:51.822
jelly baby things, some fudge.

00:05:51.822 --> 00:05:52.841
Cheers.

00:05:52.841 --> 00:05:54.758
(ding)

00:05:57.014 --> 00:05:59.302
It's the best thing I've
ever put in my mouth.

00:05:59.302 --> 00:06:01.173
It's not like an overload of chocolate.

00:06:01.173 --> 00:06:02.560
Physically heavy.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.457
- (laughing)

00:06:03.457 --> 00:06:04.890
- Taste-wise light.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:05.783
- Yeah.

00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:07.418
And the texture changes throughout.

00:06:07.418 --> 00:06:11.304
Salt, marshmallow, coconut
ice, it's more like a fudge

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.635
and the jellybeans become a sticky.

00:06:13.635 --> 00:06:14.468
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:14.468 --> 00:06:16.083
- And the honeycombs crispy.

00:06:16.083 --> 00:06:18.694
- It's like a new chocolate
bar every bite, isn't it?

00:06:18.694 --> 00:06:20.162
- It's becoming more and more difficult.

00:06:20.162 --> 00:06:21.679
- It feels slightly greedy.

00:06:21.679 --> 00:06:22.820
- But satisfying.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.574
Sorry, but this is mine.

00:06:24.574 --> 00:06:26.935
- And I mean this thing is ridiculous.

00:06:26.935 --> 00:06:27.768
Chocolate fact:

00:06:27.768 --> 00:06:30.210
- In Mayan times the cocoa bean was

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.525
actually used as currency.

00:06:31.525 --> 00:06:32.916
- What could you get for one bean?

00:06:32.916 --> 00:06:34.772
- I don't know it's like a tena.

00:06:34.772 --> 00:06:36.078
- (laughing)

00:06:36.078 --> 00:06:38.123
- But what if they were different sizes?

00:06:38.123 --> 00:06:39.549
- Oh, was that?

00:06:39.549 --> 00:06:40.448
- Well, I don't know.

00:06:40.448 --> 00:06:42.291
- Well, you need to find this stuff out.

00:06:42.291 --> 00:06:44.370
You're the fact man.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.890
- [Rich] Don't tap your head.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.973
No. (laughing)

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.773
(upbeat drums)

00:06:49.773 --> 00:06:51.780
So for this next part it's kinda weird.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.932
When researching expensive chocolate,

00:06:53.932 --> 00:06:57.353
the most expensive is from
a company called To'ak

00:06:57.353 --> 00:07:00.778
that's based in Ecuador,
you can buy it in the UK--

00:07:00.778 --> 00:07:01.611
- UK.

00:07:01.611 --> 00:07:03.709
- But Liz wouldn't let us go to Ecuador.

00:07:03.709 --> 00:07:04.891
- I'm sorry.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:06.808
- Joe, where's Ecuador?

00:07:09.864 --> 00:07:11.273
Yeah, okay.

00:07:11.273 --> 00:07:14.488
We will not reveal where
this chocolate bar is sold.

00:07:14.488 --> 00:07:16.001
We have to keep it secret.

00:07:16.001 --> 00:07:17.915
- Are we going in Harrods?

00:07:17.915 --> 00:07:19.262
- Chocolate joke.

00:07:19.262 --> 00:07:20.484
- Chocolate jokes.

00:07:20.484 --> 00:07:23.492
I was struggling to open
my chocolate Easter egg.

00:07:23.492 --> 00:07:25.492
Eventually I cracked it.

00:07:27.605 --> 00:07:28.438
- That's a good one.

00:07:28.438 --> 00:07:29.271
- That's a good one?

00:07:29.271 --> 00:07:30.104
- That's a good one.

00:07:30.104 --> 00:07:30.937
- Yeah.

00:07:30.937 --> 00:07:31.770
(cash register ding)

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:32.603
- [Evelyn] Oh my Gah--

00:07:32.603 --> 00:07:33.436
- Most expensive purchase of chocolate.

00:07:33.436 --> 00:07:34.436
- [Joe] Ohh.

00:07:35.522 --> 00:07:38.095
(beeping, ringing)

00:07:38.095 --> 00:07:38.992
- [Together] Hi!

00:07:38.992 --> 00:07:41.894
- I am Carl and I'm calling you from

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.311
To'ak headquarter in Ecuador.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.046
(cash register)

00:08:40.046 --> 00:08:44.213
- This is the most expensive
chocolate in the world!

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:47.904
- [Rich] I feel like Indiana Jones.

00:08:47.904 --> 00:08:49.166
This is so posh.

00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:52.716
Ew, that's £300 of chocolate right there.

00:08:52.716 --> 00:08:56.177
- [Evelyn] I feel like I'm touching gold.

00:08:56.177 --> 00:08:57.113
- What are these?

00:08:57.113 --> 00:08:58.047
Little tweezers.

00:08:58.047 --> 00:09:00.531
It's like this fancy
contraption is for eating the

00:09:00.531 --> 00:09:04.157
chocolate because our
hands are not worthy.

00:09:04.157 --> 00:09:06.683
Okay, let's take you off.

00:09:06.683 --> 00:09:08.284
(record scratch)

00:09:08.284 --> 00:09:12.128
- When you're eating something
so special you whisper.

00:09:12.128 --> 00:09:13.569
- (laughing)

00:09:13.569 --> 00:09:15.237
- Harvest year 2015.

00:09:15.237 --> 00:09:17.601
- Like wine there's a year for it.

00:09:17.601 --> 00:09:19.317
- Yeah, what if it's out of date?

00:09:19.317 --> 00:09:20.609
♪ Ohhhh ♪

00:09:20.609 --> 00:09:21.442
- [Evelyn] Oh my God, there's--

00:09:21.442 --> 00:09:22.275
- What is that?

00:09:22.275 --> 00:09:23.108
- A bean in the middle.

00:09:23.108 --> 00:09:24.122
What?

00:09:24.122 --> 00:09:24.955
- A bean.

00:09:25.846 --> 00:09:27.397
It's like a game of operation.

00:09:27.397 --> 00:09:28.230
(buzzer)

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.313
Look at that.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.953
I mean just for the rarity
of these beans, I think.

00:09:32.953 --> 00:09:33.786
- Are we--

00:09:33.786 --> 00:09:34.995
- Opp!

00:09:34.995 --> 00:09:35.879
- You know what's also cool?

00:09:35.879 --> 00:09:37.717
This is super expensive, right?

00:09:37.717 --> 00:09:40.081
But it is just chocolate,
they haven't done any

00:09:40.081 --> 00:09:42.439
of the gimmicks like paint it in gold or

00:09:42.439 --> 00:09:43.578
put it in a diamond.

00:09:43.578 --> 00:09:45.616
I mean the packaging is
beautiful and it's lovely,

00:09:45.616 --> 00:09:48.429
but it's much more to
do with the chocolate.

00:09:48.429 --> 00:09:50.261
(upbeat music)

00:09:50.261 --> 00:09:54.672
To me it smells like this
amazing old study with

00:09:54.672 --> 00:09:57.476
a fireplace and two big
ol' leather armchairs,

00:09:57.476 --> 00:10:01.552
like some old books and it's
all warm and cozy in there.

00:10:01.552 --> 00:10:04.540
There's a glass whiskey on
the side and there's just

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.656
this old wise dog sat by the
fire who just sorta looks up.

00:10:08.656 --> 00:10:09.660
(bark)

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:10.560
(pop)

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.478
That's what it smells like.

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:14.895
(jazz music)

00:10:19.599 --> 00:10:22.369
- Honestly, there's definitely a high.

00:10:22.369 --> 00:10:24.482
- That's why it's so expensive,
it's laced with drugs.

00:10:24.482 --> 00:10:25.866
- (laughing)

00:10:25.866 --> 00:10:28.026
- Drink wine, the initial
taste is slightly different

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:30.096
from the next taste and it changes again

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.684
and then you have an aftertaste.

00:10:31.684 --> 00:10:33.190
It's exactly the same with this.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.238
- There's fire and there's ice.

00:10:35.238 --> 00:10:36.995
There's heavy, there's light.

00:10:36.995 --> 00:10:39.081
- Yeah, I definitely got
some chocolate in there.

00:10:39.081 --> 00:10:42.267
The James Bond of chocolates,
effortlessly cool.

00:10:42.267 --> 00:10:43.902
- Quietly epic.

00:10:43.902 --> 00:10:46.535
- Quietly epic chocolate.

00:10:46.535 --> 00:10:50.087
I've got like £50 worth of
chocolate on my fingers.

00:10:50.087 --> 00:10:52.287
Which of the three
amazing chocolates was the

00:10:52.287 --> 00:10:53.470
most worth it for you?

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:57.550
- I love the way To'ak, so
much depth to the flavor.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.119
- It was like havin' an
incredible bottle of wine.

00:11:00.119 --> 00:11:01.300
- Gotta say, gotta say.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.886
The Grown Up Chocolate Company.

00:11:02.886 --> 00:11:04.809
A real chocolate factory.

00:11:04.809 --> 00:11:05.705
I loved it.

00:11:05.705 --> 00:11:09.415
- My winner Choccywoccydoodah,
so bad for you.

00:11:09.415 --> 00:11:10.642
So delicious.

00:11:10.642 --> 00:11:11.667
I'm obsessed.

00:11:11.667 --> 00:11:13.215
- And we had such a good day there.

00:11:13.215 --> 00:11:14.558
- Yeah it was a fun day--

00:11:14.558 --> 00:11:15.391
- Yeah.

00:11:15.391 --> 00:11:16.312
- Until the birds.

00:11:16.312 --> 00:11:19.528
(evil laughter)

00:11:19.528 --> 00:11:21.699
(ding)

00:11:21.699 --> 00:11:24.282
(upbeat music)

00:11:31.831 --> 00:11:35.748
(sign swinging and squeaking)

